maria.lead: Quick sync: we need a single recommended approach for the JS SDK's HTTP layer. Goal: no surprises for browser + edge, small bundle for web, predictable Node behavior (CJS+ESM). Thoughts?

jon-sdk: Prefer global fetch if present. For Node fallback -> dynamic import of undici. Keep SDK itself unopinionated by allowing injection -> init({ fetch }).

priya: Agree. Important: undici is ESM-only on newer versions; CJS consumers will be affected. We should document `const { fetch } = require('undici');` for CJS quickstarts and ship a tiny shim in sample apps.

kevin: Suggest a tiny adapter that normalizes headers/Response/Body/AbortController so retry & auth layers don't need to special-case runtimes. Example pseudo:

```js
export async function resolveFetch(provided) {
  if (provided) return provided;
  if (typeof fetch === 'function') return fetch;
  try {
    const undici = await import('undici');
    return undici.fetch || undici;
  } catch (_) {
    throw new Error('fetch missing: install undici or use node >=18 or pass fetch to init()');
  }
}
```

maria.lead: On retries: streaming responses can't be retried. Either limit retries to idempotent routes or buffer the body (with maxBytes) and clone for retry. Also propagate AbortSignal across retries.

priya: Edge variants (Cloudflare/Vercel/Deno) differ in streams and header casing. Our shim should detect `globalThis?.Deno` or cf env and pick web-like behavior.

jon-sdk: Packaging: use conditional exports + dist/ files. Add `exports` map for import/require and a `browser` field to keep web bundlers happy.

kevin: Types: export `export type FetchLike = (input: RequestInfo, init?: RequestInit) => Promise<Response>;` in a top-level types/fetch.d.ts and re-export it so customers can use our types.

maria.lead: Onboarding copy: quickstart snippets for Browser (no deps), Node ESM (node<18: `npm i undici`), Node CJS (show require example), and an inject example `init({ fetch: globalThis.fetch })`.

devex-bot: :white_check_mark: Task created DEVEX-498: "JS SDK fetch adapter + docs + samples"

maria.lead: I'll open the PR with the adapter, types, and two sample-app changes. Please add CI jobs for node14/16/18 and edge runtime smoke tests. Thanks!
